From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ieee1905: ieee1905 skip probe backhaul bsta
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

ieee1905: skip the blocking wifi probe for a registered backhaul bSTA

fix#1 (0001-ieee1905-skip-slow-wifi-dm-probes) skips the synchronous libwifi
mediainfo/WPS probe in i1905_alloc_interface() only for interfaces whose name
matches ".sta" or "ap-mld". The wireless backhaul STA registered by map-agent's
set_uplink hook (patch 0001-register-1905-wireless-backhaul-interface) is a
bare-named 4addr STA (e.g. "wlan1_0") that matches neither, so it falls through
to platform_wifi_get_mediainfo()/get_wps_status(), whose hostapd control-socket
round trips block the single ieee1905d uloop thread. (This used to say "a mt76
GET_STATION dump that never terminates"; that claim was never measured and is
wrong - see the correction in patch 0001.) While it is
stalled, the controller's 1 s-bounded ubus_invoke(..., "cmdu", ..., 1000) send
of the AP-Autoconfiguration Response / WSC M2 fails and the CMDU is dropped, so
the agent never completes onboarding (num_nodes stays 0) even though the
backhaul link and 1905 Topology Discovery are fully up.

Let the caller flag the interface: map-agent passes {"wifi_backhaul":true} to
ieee1905 add_interface; i1905_interface_add sets a transient
priv->add_iface_wifi_backhaul around the synchronous i1905_setup_interface()
call, and i1905_alloc_interface takes the same early skip as the ".sta"/"ap-mld"
cases. Single-threaded uloop makes the transient flag race-free. The AF_PACKET
socket created afterwards is all that is needed to TX/RX 1905 CMDUs on the
backhaul. HW-proven root cause 2026-07-15.

--- a/src/i1905.h	2026-07-15 18:21:51.205534420 +0200
+++ b/src/i1905.h	2026-07-15 18:21:51.219544128 +0200
@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@
 
 	bool paused;
 	int start_apconfig;
+	/* transient: set around i1905_setup_interface() from i1905_interface_add
+	 * to skip the blocking wifi mediainfo/WPS probe for a wireless backhaul
+	 * bSTA (4addr STA), whose probe blocks on the hostapd control socket. */
+	bool add_iface_wifi_backhaul;
 
 	int cmdsock;
 	char *cmdpath;
--- a/src/i1905.c	2026-07-15 18:21:51.207775770 +0200
+++ b/src/i1905.c	2026-07-15 18:21:51.219782336 +0200
@@ -364,7 +364,8 @@
 		 * even detecting it via platform_wifi_get_4addr_parent() blocks
 		 * (hostapd_cli). Detect by name (no syscall); the AF_PACKET socket
 		 * created later is all we need to RX their 1905 CMDUs. */
-		if (strstr(ifname, ".sta") || !strncmp(ifname, "ap-mld", 6)) {
+		if (priv->add_iface_wifi_backhaul ||
+		    strstr(ifname, ".sta") || !strncmp(ifname, "ap-mld", 6)) {
 			info("%s: 4addr/MLD affiliated - skip wifi probe\n", ifname);
 			n->media = I1905_MEDIA_UNKNOWN;
 			n->num_mediainfo = 0;
--- a/src/i1905_cmdresp.c	2026-07-15 18:21:51.209897334 +0200
+++ b/src/i1905_cmdresp.c	2026-07-15 18:21:51.219698880 +0200
@@ -1522,11 +1522,13 @@
 /* add/del interface policy */
 enum {
 	I1905_INTERFACE_IFNAME,		/* interface name */
+	I1905_INTERFACE_WIFI_BACKHAUL,	/* skip blocking wifi probe (backhaul bSTA) */
 	NUM_I1905_INTERFACE_POLICY,
 };
 
 static const struct blobmsg_policy interface_policy[NUM_I1905_INTERFACE_POLICY] = {
 	[I1905_INTERFACE_IFNAME] = { .name = "ifname", .type = BLOBMSG_TYPE_STRING },
+	[I1905_INTERFACE_WIFI_BACKHAUL] = { .name = "wifi_backhaul", .type = BLOBMSG_TYPE_BOOL },
 };
 
 int i1905_interface_add(struct i1905_private *priv, void *args, void *out)
@@ -1554,7 +1556,16 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/* Skip the blocking wifi mediainfo/WPS probe in i1905_alloc_interface for a
+	 * wireless backhaul bSTA (4addr STA): its GET_STATION dump never returns on
+	 * mt76 and stalls this uloop thread, starving the 1 s-bounded "cmdu" invoke
+	 * the controller uses to send AP-Autoconfig Response / WSC M2 -> onboarding
+	 * stalls forever. Single-threaded uloop makes the transient flag race-free. */
+	if (tb[I1905_INTERFACE_WIFI_BACKHAUL])
+		priv->add_iface_wifi_backhaul =
+			blobmsg_get_bool(tb[I1905_INTERFACE_WIFI_BACKHAUL]);
 	iface = i1905_setup_interface(priv, ifname);
+	priv->add_iface_wifi_backhaul = false;
 	if (!iface) {
 		dbg("%s: %s: error setup interface\n", __func__, ifname);
 		ret = 1;
